      {
        "title": "Jehoiakim's Last Years",
        "introduction": "Jehoiakim must have a death wish. He has callously burned God's written Word, and now, with the strength of a mouse pursuing a lion, Jehoiakim has the audacity to rebel against Nebuchadnezzar. Fortunately for Judah, Nebuchadnezzar does not react with immediate military force, at least not directly. However, he may well be the motivating force behind the attacks against Judah by several of its neighbors over a four-year period of inconclusive war. Jehoiakim is destined to live his last days in wearying conflict."
      },
      {
        "title": "",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "title": "Jehoiakim Attempts Rebellion",
            "references": [
              {
                "book": "2 Kings",
                "chapter": 24,
                "verse": "1b"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Judah's Neighbors Harass",
            "references": [
              {
                "book": "2 Kings",
                "chapter": 24,
                "verse": "2-4"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
